    "q-179426": {
      "dom_id": "step-q179426",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(B)=0.65,$ and $P(A\\cap B)=0.35,$ find $P(A\\cup B).$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275667/assets/35e807b7de787f50d0cbff770e4083cef84b4d35030b4c506b1db5646cf7a358.png)\n\nThe addition law for probability states that\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B).\n$$\n\nSo, to calculate $P(A\\cup B),$ we apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.5+0.65-0.35 \\\\  & =0.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Venn diagram corresponding to this situation is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275667/assets/3e2a6752a28ddcfc678e24cb681de5730d5765d8cea45c741ae9783339449770.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
